    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "The test hinges on reproducing published mlotst from thetao and so, so the exact mlotst definition—surface-referenced sigma-t/buoyancy criterion at local pressure and online computation then monthly averaging—directly constrains the operator MLD being compared.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the offline operator with `ref_depth` equal to the model's shallowest level (not 10 m), using each monthly `thetao`/`so` profile and linear interpolation of the threshold crossing; compare monthly operator MLDs with published `mlotst` only after forming the March/September climatologies from those monthly MLDs.",
        "State that residual disagreement is diagnostic, not model error: `mlotst` uses the model top level, a displaced-parcel density test at local pressure, and the monthly mean of instantaneous MLDs; an offline MLD from monthly `thetao`/`so` is therefore expected to be shallower than `mlotst`, and cells where the threshold is never reached must be excluded from operator-versus-`mlotst` comparison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The user proposes computing MLD offline from monthly thetao and so and comparing with monthly mlotst, and this fragment says nonlinear diagnostics like MLD computed from monthly means differ from the online diagnostic and from the monthly mean of that diagnostic, which must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Do diagnostic first, then average: compute MLD from each monthly `thetao`/`so` field for every March and September, then average those 30 monthly MLDs; do not compute MLD from a 1971-2000 March or September mean profile.",
        "For the 1971-2000 climatologies, a calendar-month climatology is the plain mean of that month across years; do not day-weight across the 30 Marches or 30 Septembers."
      ]
    },
