      "reason": "The requested bias, RMSE, correlation, exceedance area and cross-model ranking all require using the same valid-data mask for the fields being compared, and the summary specifically covers shared-domain masking for cell-by-cell comparisons and rankings.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put each pair of fields for mapping/scatter on one grid, then build one shared valid-data mask over operator MLD and `mlotst` and apply it to both before bias, RMSE, correlation, or exceedance-area are computed; report the mask cell counts/area coverage with the metrics.",
        "The question’s definition is stricter than a pairwise monthly mask: both climatologies must cover only cells where both fields are defined in all 30 instances of that month, so enforce that all-30-month shared mask before taking the climatologies and metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "The analysis will read thetao, so, mlotst and areacello over full ocean grids, and this fragment warns that unmasked CMIP6 missing values over land/below seafloor can silently corrupt means, RMSDs and area fractions.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use NaN-aware masking/reductions throughout; if any read path exposes `1e20`, treat it as missing before any arithmetic, or sums/means/RMSE become meaningless.",
        "Build the valid mask from each field itself, not from another variable or a land mask alone, because masks can differ between variables of the same model."
      ]
    },
    {
